WEBVTT

00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:13.050
Seventy-six thousand seven hundred and seven MAID deaths between 2016 and 2024 — rising from one thousand and eighteen in 2016 to sixteen thousand four hundred and ninety-nine in 2024.

00:00:13.000 --> 00:00:16.204
A fifteen hundred and twenty percent increase.

00:00:16.204 --> 00:00:20.556
MAID now accounts for five point one percent of all Canadian deaths.

00:00:20.556 --> 00:00:26.374
Seven hundred and thirty-two Track 2 non-terminal MAID deaths were recorded in 2024 alone.

00:00:26.374 --> 00:00:32.409
Forty-seven thousand opioid overdose deaths between 2016 and 2023.

00:00:32.409 --> 00:00:37.284
Approximately ten thousand estimated excess deaths from housing and homelessness.

00:00:37.284 --> 00:00:41.318
Four thousand five hundred veteran suicides since 2000.

00:00:41.318 --> 00:00:46.215
Over five thousand long-term care COVID deaths attributable to policy failures.

00:00:46.215 --> 00:00:53.761
This is the Policy Harm Index — a comprehensive registry of Canadian legislative changes with measurable, preventable death tolls.

00:00:53.761 --> 00:00:55.818
Every number is sourced.

00:00:55.818 --> 00:00:58.034
Every policy is named.

00:00:58.034 --> 00:01:01.227
Every death was counted by the government that caused it.
